  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "en",
      "_type": "object",
      "value": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000001",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "wdrqc8px4x8p",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Unveiling the Mysteries of Al-Qasr: A Timeless Islamic Village in "
            },
            {
              "_key": "8trsfyl6jrur",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "nstetz8janfw"
              ],
              "text": "Dakhla Oasis"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "nstetz8janfw",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58783",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000002",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Nestled in the heart of Egypt’s "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000004",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000003"
              ],
              "text": "Dakhla Oasis"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000005",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", Al-Qasr village stands as a remarkable testament to Islamic heritage, renowned as the most intact Islamic village still in existence. Located northwest of Mut, along the Sioh Ridge, Al-Qasr majestically defines the northern boundary of the oasis. Its continuous habitation and exceptional preservation make it unparalleled among settlements in Dakhla."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000003",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "http://travel2egypt.org/egypt-travel-guide/dakhla-oasis/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/dakhla-oasis",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000b",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000007",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Believed to have been founded by "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000009",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000008"
              ],
              "text": "the Ayyubids"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " towards the late 12th century, Al-Qasr (literally ‘The Fortress’) evolved from the remnants of a Roman settlement. Its strategic position and fortified structure were ingeniously designed to ward off invading armies from the west and south."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000008",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayyubid_dynasty",
              "newTab": true
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000d",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The village’s narrow, shaded streets, reminiscent of the ancient town of Mut, are divided into quarters, each historically secured at night by gated fences. While the passage of time has brought changes, Al-Qasr has retained its distinctive three-story mudbrick minaret, which towers 21 meters above the mosque of Nasr el-Din from the Ayyubid era. This minaret is a solitary survivor from the original mosque; the rest was reconstructed in the 19th century."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000f",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Within the mosque lies the mausoleum of Sheikh Nasr el-Din, adorned with beautifully inscribed wooden lintels above the entrances. The ancient madrasa, once a center for Quranic learning, has evolved into a multifunctional school and public meeting place, open for visitors to explore."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000011",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000010",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Another highlight for visitors is the meticulously preserved Abu Nafir’s house, a towering structure with a heavy wooden door crafted from a Ptolemaic temple. The door jambs, featuring a melange of symbols, predominantly from repurposed blocks, narrate stories from a bygone era."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000013",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000012",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Wandering through the cool, meandering alleyways of Al-Qasr, one is treated to spectacular views of intricately carved lintels and beams that grace the entrances of many houses, blending ancient artistry with modern aesthetics."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000015",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000014",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The village is rich in historical inscriptions, with the oldest found on Beit Ibrahim, dating back to the 15th century. Recent discoveries, including a corn-mill and pottery factory furnaces, hint at a vibrant post-antiquity community. Today, nearly 700 residents, predominantly craftsmen, call Al-Qasr home, renowned for their skill in creating earthenware pots and palm-leaf baskets."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000017",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000016",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Interestingly, those who leave Al-Qasr cannot return to reside, as the Ministry of Antiquities claims deserted houses, and new construction is prohibited, preserving the village’s historical integrity."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000019",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000018",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Under the Dakhla Oasis Project, Al-Qasr has been the focus of extensive archaeological study and restoration efforts. Investigations have revealed the possibility of a pre-existing Roman fortress beneath the village, with some suggesting that the Roman camp, Takastra, lies beneath today’s Al-Qasr."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Al-Qasr, with its rich tapestry of history, architecture, and craftsmanship, offers a unique window into the "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000001b"
              ],
              "text": "Islamic era"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " of Egypt, standing as a beacon of cultural preservation and historical continuity in the stunning landscape of the Dakhla Oasis."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001b",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "http://travel2egypt.org/tours/the-grand-islamic-day-tour/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/the-grand-islamic-day-tour",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001f",
          "_pendingImage": "https://travel2egypt.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/dakhla-oasis-trips-in-egypt.jpg",
          "_type": "image",
          "alt": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "dakhla oasis travel guide"
            }
          ],
          "caption": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "The historic minaret of the Nasr El Din Mosque rises over the Dakhla Oasis, embodying the enduring spirit of Egypt's heartland deserts"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000020",
          "_pendingImage": "https://travel2egypt.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Dakhla-e1554945660393-1200x900-1.jpg",
          "_type": "image",
          "alt": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "dakhla oasis travel guide"
            }
          ],
          "caption": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "Weathered elegance: a balcony stands defiantly amidst the crumbling relics of a bygone era"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "es",
      "_type": "object",
      "value": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000001",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "eiwngillfdbh",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Sólo aquí en el Oasis de "
            },
            {
              "_key": "cno1c1csvrm6",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "ob7hylhk9qpu"
              ],
              "text": "Dakhla"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "ob7hylhk9qpu",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58783",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000009",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000002",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Enclavada en el corazón del "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000004",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000003"
              ],
              "text": "oasis"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000005",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " egipcio "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000007",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000006"
              ],
              "text": "de Dakhla"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000008",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", la aldea de Al-Qasr es un notable testimonio de la herencia islámica, reconocida como la aldea islámica más intacta que aún existe. Situada al noroeste de Mut, a lo largo de la Cresta de Sioh, Al-Qasr define majestuosamente el límite septentrional del oasis. Su habitación continua y su excepcional conservación hacen que no tenga parangón entre los asentamientos de Dajla."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000003",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://travel2egypt1.wpenginepowered.com/egypt-travel-guide/dakhla-oasis/",
              "newTab": true
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000006",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://travel2egypt1.wpenginepowered.com/egypt-travel-guide/dakhla-oasis/",
              "newTab": true
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000011",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Se cree que fue fundada por "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000000b"
              ],
              "text": "los ayubíes"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " hacia finales del siglo XII, Al-Qasr (literalmente «La Fortaleza») evolucionó a partir de los restos de un asentamiento romano. Su posición estratégica y su estructura fortificada fueron ingeniosamente diseñadas para rechazar a "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000000e"
              ],
              "text": "los ejércitos invasores del"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000010",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " oeste y el sur."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000b",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayyubid_dynasty",
              "newTab": true
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000e",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/guia-de-viaje-de-al-fayoum/la-piramide-de-al-lahun/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/es/guide/al-fayoum/la-piramide-de-al-lahun",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000019",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000012",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Las calles estrechas y sombreadas del pueblo, "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000014",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000013"
              ],
              "text": "que recuerdan a la antigua ciudad"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000015",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " de Mut, están divididas en barrios, cada uno de ellos históricamente protegido por la noche con vallas. Aunque el paso del tiempo ha traído cambios, Al-Qasr ha conservado su característico minarete de adobe de tres pisos, que se eleva 21 metros sobre la mezquita de Nasr "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000017",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000016"
              ],
              "text": "el-Din de la época ayyubí"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000018",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ". Este minarete es un superviviente solitario de la mezquita original; el resto se reconstruyó en el siglo XIX."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000013",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/guia-de-viaje-de-guiza/menfis-la-ciudad-antigua/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/guia-de-viaje-de-guiza/menfis-la-ciudad-antigua/",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000016",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/guia-de-viaje-de-el-cairo/madrasa-y-mausoleo-de-as-salih-negm-el-din-ayyub/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/es/guide/cairo/madrasa-y-mausoleo-de-as-salih-negm-el-din-ayyub",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000021",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Dentro de la "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000001b"
              ],
              "text": "mezquita se encuentra el mausoleo del"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " jeque Nasr el-Din, adornado con dinteles de madera bellamente inscritos sobre las entradas. La antigua madrasa, que en su día fue un centro de aprendizaje coránico, ha evolucionado hasta convertirse en una escuela multifuncional y un lugar de reunión público, abierto a los "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000001e"
              ],
              "text": "visitantes para que"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000020",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " lo exploren."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001b",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/guia-de-viaje-de-el-cairo/mezquita-del-sheij-al-muayyad/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/es/guide/cairo/mezquita-del-sheij-al-muayyad",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001e",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/vacaciones-inolvidables-en-egipto/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/es/blog/vacaciones-inolvidables-en-egipto",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000029",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000022",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Otro punto "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000024",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000023"
              ],
              "text": "destacado"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000025",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " para los visitantes es la casa de Abu Nafir, meticulosamente conservada, una imponente estructura con una pesada puerta de madera procedente de un templo ptolemaico. Las jambas de las puertas, con una mezcla de símbolos, principalmente de bloques reutilizados, narran "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000027",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000026"
              ],
              "text": "historias"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000028",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " de una época pasada."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000023",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/guia-de-viaje-de-suez/destacados/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/guia-de-viaje-de-suez/destacados/",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000026",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/explorando-la-gran-esfinge-de-guiza/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/es/blog/explorando-la-gran-esfinge-de-guiza",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000002e",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000002a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Deambulando por las frescas y serpenteantes callejuelas de Al-Qasr, se disfruta de espectaculares vistas de dinteles y vigas intrincadamente tallados que adornan las entradas de muchas casas, mezclando el "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000002c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000002b"
              ],
              "text": "arte antiguo con"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000002d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " la estética moderna."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000002b",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/el-tiempo-en-egipto/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/es/guide/rosetta-rasheed/el-tiempo-en-rosetta-rashid-y-la-mejor-epoca-para-visitarla",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000033",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000002f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "El pueblo es rico en inscripciones históricas, la más antigua "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000031",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000030"
              ],
              "text": "de las"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000032",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " cuales se encuentra en Beit Ibrahim y data del siglo XV. Descubrimientos recientes, como un molino de maíz y hornos de una fábrica de cerámica, apuntan a una vibrante comunidad posterior a la Antigüedad. En la actualidad, cerca de 700 residentes, en su mayoría artesanos, consideran Al-Qasr su hogar, famoso por su habilidad en la creación de vasijas de barro y cestas de hoja de palmera."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000030",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/itinerario-de-1-dia-por-las-piramides-de-guiza-disfruta-de-las-maravillas-del-antiguo-egipto/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/es/blog/itinerario-de-1-dia-por-las-piramides-de-guiza-disfruta-de-las-maravillas-del-antiguo-egipto",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000038",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000034",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Curiosamente, quienes abandonan Al-Qasr no pueden volver a residir, ya que el Ministerio de Antigüedades reclama las casas desiertas, y se prohíben las nuevas construcciones, lo "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000036",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000035"
              ],
              "text": "que preserva la integridad histórica del"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000037",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " pueblo."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000035",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/lugares-historicos-del-sinai/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/es/blog/lugares-historicos-del-sinai",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000040",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000039",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "En el marco "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000003b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000003a"
              ],
              "text": "del Proyecto Oasis"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000003c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " de Dajla, Al-Qasr ha sido objeto de amplios estudios arqueológicos y esfuerzos de restauración. Las investigaciones han revelado la posibilidad de una "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000003e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000003d"
              ],
              "text": "fortaleza romana"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000003f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " preexistente bajo la aldea, y algunos sugieren que el campamento romano de Takastra se encuentra bajo la actual Al-Qasr."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000003a",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
